  "notes": "AA-LCR is Artificial Analysis's long-context reasoning benchmark. It ships 100 human-crafted questions that each require reading roughly 100K input tokens and then reasoning across several documents to arrive at a single correct answer. The dataset draws from seven real-world document categories (company reports, industry reports, government consultations, academic papers, legal documents, marketing materials, survey reports); the corpus is about 3M tokens spanning 30 document sets and 234 documents.\n\nScoring is pass@1 accuracy. A candidate answer is compared against a human-verified reference by an LLM equality checker (Qwen3 235B A22B 2507 in non-reasoning mode). Human first-attempt accuracy is reported at 40 to 60 percent.\n\nAA-LCR is one component of the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index. There is no academic paper or public code repository from the benchmark authors, so the `paper` field is null; `github` points at the merged Harbor adapter, the only open-source implementation against this benchmark.\n\nResults in this file cover the 2025-08 launch through 2026-04, reconstructed from AA's leaderboard page (current and archived snapshots) and the launch announcement blog, plus the Harbor adapter's parity runs. All scores originate with Artificial Analysis itself."
}